WEBVTT

00:00:02.869 --> 00:00:04.734
Good afternoon, Ensign.

00:00:04.771 --> 00:00:06.636
How are we doing today?

00:00:06.673 --> 00:00:09.403
We're doing just fine,
thank you.

00:00:09.442 --> 00:00:11.672
Good, good.

00:00:11.711 --> 00:00:14.475
By the way, I was wondering
if you'd take a look

00:00:14.581 --> 00:00:16.708
at the thermal array
in the kitchen.

00:00:16.750 --> 00:00:18.240
It overloaded this morning

00:00:18.284 --> 00:00:20.309
and vaporized
an entire pot roast.

00:00:20.353 --> 00:00:21.581
I'd be happy to.

00:00:21.621 --> 00:00:23.851
Wonderful. My!

00:00:23.890 --> 00:00:25.790
I informed Ensign Kim
about the problem hours ago

00:00:25.825 --> 00:00:28.259
and he still hasn't
come down to fix it.

00:00:28.294 --> 00:00:30.125
He's been working on a problem

00:00:30.163 --> 00:00:32.290
with the structural
integrity grid.

00:00:32.332 --> 00:00:34.732
I'm sure he hasn't
forgotten about you.

00:00:34.768 --> 00:00:36.633
If this thing doesn't
get fixed soon,

00:00:36.669 --> 00:00:38.728
we'll all be eating
cold leftovers for dinner,

00:00:38.772 --> 00:00:40.364
and who do you think
the crew will blame?

00:00:40.407 --> 00:00:42.375
Mm.

00:00:42.409 --> 00:00:44.377
Looks like you need a new
set of anodyne relays.

00:00:45.412 --> 00:00:46.379
I'll go down to Engineering

00:00:46.413 --> 00:00:47.675
and get some for you
out of storage.

00:00:47.714 --> 00:00:49.113
Thanks.

00:00:49.149 --> 00:00:52.710
Oh, and while you're here,
would you mind taking a look

00:00:52.752 --> 00:00:53.912
at the replicator?

00:00:53.953 --> 00:00:56.513
It's been having
trouble making anything

00:00:56.556 --> 00:00:58.615
with large amounts
of cellulose.

00:00:58.658 --> 00:00:59.716
Of course.

00:00:59.759 --> 00:01:01.693
Cabbage, psyllium,

00:01:01.728 --> 00:01:03.889
green beans, celery,
it all comes out

00:01:03.930 --> 00:01:05.625
looking a touch too yellow.

00:01:05.665 --> 00:01:07.724
I thought you didn't
use replicated vegetables

00:01:07.767 --> 00:01:08.961
when you're cooking.

00:01:09.002 --> 00:01:11.800
Always fresh, organic,
from the airponic bay?

00:01:11.838 --> 00:01:14.898
Uh, well, the yields
have been a little low lately.

00:01:14.941 --> 00:01:19.344
Normally, I would never dream
of using synthesized veggies.

00:01:19.379 --> 00:01:22.348
It looks like a malfunction
in the power grid.

00:01:22.382 --> 00:01:24.475
Shouldn't be too difficult...

00:01:26.686 --> 00:01:28.415
What's wrong?

00:01:28.455 --> 00:01:30.685
I think I'm having
a contraction.

00:01:30.723 --> 00:01:33.886
Oh, yeah, it's a contraction,
all right.

00:01:33.927 --> 00:01:35.121
Well, that's wonderful.

00:01:35.161 --> 00:01:37.459
Labor can't be far behind.

00:01:37.497 --> 00:01:40.159
Let's... let's get you
to Sick Bay.

00:01:40.200 --> 00:01:42.760
Try to breathe, now...
deep, deep regular breaths.

00:01:42.802 --> 00:01:44.497
Not so fast now.

00:01:44.537 --> 00:01:46.698
We're having a baby!

00:01:47.707 --> 00:01:49.072
- That's good.
- Hmm.

00:01:49.109 --> 00:01:50.041
Push!

00:01:53.413 --> 00:01:54.846
Don't forget to breathe,
Samantha.

00:01:54.881 --> 00:01:57.281
Deep regular breaths.

00:01:57.317 --> 00:01:58.545
That's it.

00:02:00.386 --> 00:02:02.411
Cervical dilation is
at 10.2 centimeters.

00:02:02.455 --> 00:02:04.150
Prostaglandin levels are normal.

00:02:04.190 --> 00:02:05.418
Push, Ensign!

00:02:05.458 --> 00:02:06.755
You push, damn it!

00:02:06.793 --> 00:02:08.454
I'm sick of pushing!

00:02:08.495 --> 00:02:09.928
I know you're fatigued.

00:02:09.963 --> 00:02:11.931
Try to focus on your breathing.

00:02:11.965 --> 00:02:13.865
Remember the exercises we did.

00:02:13.900 --> 00:02:16.460
When you feel a contraction,
bear down.

00:02:36.055 --> 00:02:37.181
This is ridiculous.

00:02:37.223 --> 00:02:38.485
It's been seven hours.

00:02:38.591 --> 00:02:40.991
How long does it take
to deliver a baby?

00:02:41.027 --> 00:02:43.291
As long as it takes, Mr. Paris.

00:02:43.329 --> 00:02:44.887
Indeed.

00:02:44.931 --> 00:02:46.990
During the birth
of our third child,

00:02:47.033 --> 00:02:49.092
my wife was in labor
for 96 hours.

00:02:49.135 --> 00:02:50.693
Four days?

00:02:50.737 --> 00:02:54.605
I have learned that pregnancy
and patience go hand-in-hand.

00:02:54.641 --> 00:02:57.337
You know, I didn't
expect to be this nervous.

00:02:57.377 --> 00:02:58.776
It's not even my child.

00:02:58.811 --> 00:03:01.974
In a way, this child
belongs to all of us.

00:03:02.015 --> 00:03:04.745
It is the first baby
born on Voyager.

00:03:04.784 --> 00:03:06.149
I'm just not sure whether

00:03:06.186 --> 00:03:08.814
I should be welcoming it
on board or apologizing.

00:03:08.855 --> 00:03:10.288
Captain?

00:03:10.323 --> 00:03:13.622
Voyager isn't exactly
anyone's idea of a nursery,

00:03:13.660 --> 00:03:17.061
and the Delta Quadrant
isn't much of a playground.

00:03:17.096 --> 00:03:19.189
My father had a saying, Captain:

00:03:19.232 --> 00:03:21.632
"Home is
wherever you happen to be."

00:03:21.668 --> 00:03:23.932
Captain, long-range sensors

00:03:23.970 --> 00:03:26.598
are picking up heavy subspace
communications ahead.

00:03:26.639 --> 00:03:27.901
They're Vidiian.

00:03:27.941 --> 00:03:29.135
All stop.
A ship?

00:03:29.175 --> 00:03:31.939
At least 20 ships
within sensor range.

00:03:31.978 --> 00:03:35.004
I am also detecting
a G-type star system

00:03:35.048 --> 00:03:36.948
with two inhabited planets.

00:03:36.983 --> 00:03:38.382
Life signs... Vidiian.

00:03:38.418 --> 00:03:40.215
Sounds like we're headed
right into their territory.

00:03:40.253 --> 00:03:42.915
And I'm in no mood
to donate any organs today.

00:03:42.956 --> 00:03:44.389
Options, Mr. Paris.

00:03:44.424 --> 00:03:48.793
There's a large plasma drift,
bearing 40 mark 7.

00:03:48.828 --> 00:03:51.490
It extends almost half
the length of this sector.

00:03:51.531 --> 00:03:53.089
Interference from the plasma

00:03:53.132 --> 00:03:54.622
should block us
from their sensors.

00:03:54.667 --> 00:03:55.634
Good thinking.

00:03:55.668 --> 00:03:57.101
Lay in a course at full impulse.

00:03:57.136 --> 00:03:59.036
Mr. Tuvok,
deflectors at maximum.

00:04:12.151 --> 00:04:13.618
Oh!

00:04:13.653 --> 00:04:15.280
Oh, what was that?!

00:04:15.321 --> 00:04:16.879
What's wrong?

00:04:16.923 --> 00:04:19.448
A pain... in my abdomen.

00:04:19.525 --> 00:04:21.891
It's different... sharp.

00:04:21.928 --> 00:04:23.225
Oh, God!

00:04:23.263 --> 00:04:25.094
The baby has shifted position

00:04:25.131 --> 00:04:28.464
and its exocranial ridges have
lodged in the uterine wall.

00:04:28.534 --> 00:04:30.126
This is a rare complication,

00:04:30.169 --> 00:04:32.569
but it's been known to happen
in human-Ktarian pregnancies.

00:04:32.605 --> 00:04:33.833
Can we reposition the baby?

00:04:33.873 --> 00:04:35.431
No, its spinal column
is too fragile.

00:04:35.475 --> 00:04:36.908
I don't want
to risk nerve damage.

00:04:39.045 --> 00:04:40.842
If we don't
deliver the baby now,

00:04:40.880 --> 00:04:42.905
its ridges could
perforate the uterus

00:04:42.949 --> 00:04:44.439
and cause internal bleeding.

00:04:44.484 --> 00:04:46.452
Kes, prepare
for a fetal transport.

00:04:47.820 --> 00:04:50.687
We're clearing
the Vidiian system, Captain.

00:04:50.723 --> 00:04:54.921
Take us out of the plasma drift
and resume our previous course.

00:04:54.961 --> 00:04:57.395
I've locked onto
the baby's coordinates.

00:04:57.430 --> 00:04:59.489
We're ready to begin.

00:04:59.532 --> 00:05:02.000
Initiating umbilical separation.

00:05:02.035 --> 00:05:03.195
Energizing.

00:05:11.944 --> 00:05:14.435
Congratulations, Ensign.

00:05:14.480 --> 00:05:16.641
It's a girl.

00:05:23.122 --> 00:05:24.680
Is she all right?

00:05:25.792 --> 00:05:28.090
The transport caused a slight
hemocythemic imbalance,

00:05:28.127 --> 00:05:30.687
but we'll stabilize
her cell membranes

00:05:30.730 --> 00:05:32.493
with osmotic pressure therapy.

00:05:35.234 --> 00:05:36.292
What was that?

00:05:36.336 --> 00:05:38.770
We hit some kind of
subspace turbulence

00:05:38.805 --> 00:05:40.864
as we were coming out
of the plasma drift.

00:05:40.907 --> 00:05:41.999
I can't tell if...

00:05:43.976 --> 00:05:45.238
What the hell?

00:05:45.278 --> 00:05:48.145
Captain, the warp engines
just stalled.

00:05:48.181 --> 00:05:49.273
Go to impulse.

00:05:49.315 --> 00:05:51.215
Impulse engines
aren't responding.

00:05:51.250 --> 00:05:53.912
Maneuvering thrusters
are out, too.

00:05:53.953 --> 00:05:54.920
We're losing main power.

00:05:54.954 --> 00:05:57.286
Switching to backup power.

00:05:57.323 --> 00:05:58.881
Red Alert.
Bridge to Engineering.

00:05:58.925 --> 00:06:00.153
Report.

00:06:00.193 --> 00:06:01.854
Our antimatter supply is
being drained, Captain.

00:06:01.894 --> 00:06:02.861
I don't know why.

00:06:02.895 --> 00:06:04.556
The containment fields
are in place.

00:06:04.597 --> 00:06:06.565
It's like we sprung a leak,
but I can't find the crack.

00:06:06.599 --> 00:06:08.999
B'Elanna,
try infusing the warp core

00:06:09.035 --> 00:06:10.559
with repeated proton bursts.

00:06:10.603 --> 00:06:12.696
That should be enough
to keep it going.

00:06:12.739 --> 00:06:15.230
I think I can generate enough
protons in the sensor array

00:06:15.274 --> 00:06:16.434
for a burst every 30 seconds.

00:06:16.509 --> 00:06:17.441
Do it.

00:06:17.543 --> 00:06:19.374
Hogan, these proton bursts

00:06:19.412 --> 00:06:21.642
are going to cause a lot
of stress on the hull.

00:06:21.681 --> 00:06:23.046
Reinforce structural
integrity to...

00:06:24.417 --> 00:06:26.317
Now what?

00:06:29.789 --> 00:06:31.086
What was that?

00:06:31.124 --> 00:06:33.092
It appeared to be
a proton burst.

00:06:33.126 --> 00:06:34.218
Already?

00:06:34.260 --> 00:06:35.591
Bridge to Torres, report.

00:06:36.596 --> 00:06:38.587
Engineering, respond.

00:06:38.631 --> 00:06:42.260
Captain, three EPS conduits
just ruptured in Engineering.

00:06:42.301 --> 00:06:43.859
They took heavy casualties.

00:06:47.340 --> 00:06:49.774
The incubator is losing power.

00:06:49.809 --> 00:06:51.777
Activate the auxiliary
respirator.

00:06:55.748 --> 00:06:57.773
We've got wounded here!

00:08:50.361 --> 00:08:52.886
Second-degree plasma burns
on the face and neck.

00:08:52.930 --> 00:08:54.921
Treat him
with the dermaline gel.

00:08:54.966 --> 00:08:57.332
Fractured clavicle,
thoracic contusions.

00:08:57.368 --> 00:08:59.199
Nothing serious, she can wait.

00:08:59.237 --> 00:09:01.569
Fused vertebrae,
prep him for surgery.

00:09:01.606 --> 00:09:02.573
Status.

00:09:02.607 --> 00:09:03.631
It doesn't look good, Doctor.

00:09:03.674 --> 00:09:05.266
The baby's cell membranes
won't stabilize.

00:09:05.309 --> 00:09:07.174
Increase the osmotic...

00:09:10.414 --> 00:09:11.608
That's not helping.

00:09:11.649 --> 00:09:13.810
Increase the osmotic
pressure ratio by ten percent.

00:09:13.851 --> 00:09:15.113
Bridge to Sick Bay.

00:09:15.152 --> 00:09:17.882
There's been a major
coolant leak in the Mess Hall.

00:09:17.922 --> 00:09:19.355
You've got more wounded
on the way.

00:09:19.390 --> 00:09:21.415
Acknowledged.

00:09:22.760 --> 00:09:24.421
Torres to Bridge!

00:09:24.462 --> 00:09:25.429
We're definitely being...

00:09:26.664 --> 00:09:29.189
We're definitely being
hit by proton bursts,

00:09:29.233 --> 00:09:31.793
but I don't know
where they're coming from.

00:09:31.836 --> 00:09:33.895
I never even started
the procedure.

00:09:33.938 --> 00:09:36.930
She's right; the main
sensor array is off-line.

00:09:36.974 --> 00:09:38.032
Not a single burst was fired.

00:09:38.075 --> 00:09:39.440
And yet the bursts appear
to be originating

00:09:39.544 --> 00:09:40.442
from within the ship.

00:09:40.545 --> 00:09:42.206
It's like they're coming out
of thin air.

00:09:42.246 --> 00:09:43.440
Captain, these bursts
are weakening

00:09:43.514 --> 00:09:44.606
the structural integrity
of the hull.

00:09:44.649 --> 00:09:45.707
We cannot take any more.

00:09:45.750 --> 00:09:48.742
Can we increase power
to structural reinforcement?

00:09:48.786 --> 00:09:50.981
Our antimatter supply
is too low.

00:09:51.022 --> 00:09:53.013
There's just not
enough power to go...

00:09:54.926 --> 00:09:57.895
Hull breach on Deck 15,
Section 29-Alpha.

00:09:57.929 --> 00:09:59.760
Emergency force fields
are off-line.

00:09:59.797 --> 00:10:01.094
Captain, I've been
working on a way

00:10:01.132 --> 00:10:03.293
to enhance our portable
force field generators.

00:10:03.334 --> 00:10:04.631
It might be enough
to seal that breach.

00:10:04.669 --> 00:10:05.727
Go.

00:10:09.874 --> 00:10:11.398
Don't you worry.

00:10:11.442 --> 00:10:14.240
We have the best doctor
in the Quadrant.

00:10:14.278 --> 00:10:16.473
Doctor, her cell membranes
are losing cohesion.

00:10:16.547 --> 00:10:18.242
Try remodulating
the osmotic pressure.

00:10:22.086 --> 00:10:23.075
No effect.

00:10:23.120 --> 00:10:25.680
Hang on, I'll be right there.

00:10:35.533 --> 00:10:36.727
Oh, no.

00:10:36.767 --> 00:10:39.099
Jefferies tube 12 runs
right over the breach.

00:10:39.136 --> 00:10:40.967
If we can get close enough,
we should be able

00:10:41.005 --> 00:10:42.495
to set up a portable
containment field.

00:10:42.573 --> 00:10:43.938
The breach has
weakened the integrity

00:10:43.975 --> 00:10:44.999
of that tube by 22 percent.

00:10:45.042 --> 00:10:46.703
That's why we need
to reinforce the field.

00:10:46.744 --> 00:10:48.371
We'll use the power
conduits on this deck.

00:10:54.251 --> 00:10:56.515
I've analyzed the bursts
on all spectral frequencies.

00:10:56.587 --> 00:10:58.521
There's still no indication
of where they're coming from.

00:10:58.556 --> 00:10:59.750
At this point,

00:10:59.790 --> 00:11:01.348
I don't give a damn
where they're coming from.

00:11:01.392 --> 00:11:02.359
I just want to stop them.

00:11:02.393 --> 00:11:03.883
Chakotay, do we have
enough auxiliary power

00:11:03.928 --> 00:11:04.952
to magnetize the hull?

00:11:04.996 --> 00:11:06.395
It might cushion the impact
of the bursts.

00:11:06.430 --> 00:11:07.624
We have just barely enough.

00:11:07.665 --> 00:11:10.190
Give it a try.

00:11:10.234 --> 00:11:11.292
I've stabilized
my imaging array,

00:11:11.335 --> 00:11:12.393
but it could go out at any time.

00:11:12.436 --> 00:11:13.403
Doctor...

00:11:13.437 --> 00:11:14.904
Prepare for emergency
resuscitation.

00:11:14.939 --> 00:11:16.463
My baby, she...

00:11:16.507 --> 00:11:19.271
she's going to die, isn't she?

00:11:19.310 --> 00:11:21.039
Not if I can help it.

00:11:26.150 --> 00:11:27.378
Here it is.

00:11:27.418 --> 00:11:29.113
The breach is directly below us.

00:11:32.423 --> 00:11:34.891
Make it fast, Harry.

00:11:34.925 --> 00:11:37.621
Torres to Hogan.
What's your status?

00:11:37.662 --> 00:11:39.129
Almost got it, Lieutenant.

00:11:39.163 --> 00:11:42.155
I'm rerouting all power
in this section to your...

00:11:47.538 --> 00:11:49.028
Torres to Hogan.

00:11:49.073 --> 00:11:50.165
Hogan, are you there?

00:11:51.542 --> 00:11:53.169
I'm hurt.

00:11:53.210 --> 00:11:54.404
Hurry.
We have to help him.

00:11:54.445 --> 00:11:56.538
Just give me a minute.

00:11:59.250 --> 00:12:01.582
Again!

00:12:01.619 --> 00:12:03.450
Nothing.

00:12:11.095 --> 00:12:12.824
I'm sorry, Ensign.

00:12:19.236 --> 00:12:21.830
Hogan to Sick Bay.

00:12:21.872 --> 00:12:25.000
I need... medical assistance...

00:12:25.042 --> 00:12:27.340
Deck 15, Section 29.

00:12:27.378 --> 00:12:28.606
I'll go.

00:12:33.317 --> 00:12:35.751
The breach is widening.
Let's get out of here.

00:12:37.755 --> 00:12:39.347
Damn it, Harry, let's go!

00:12:39.390 --> 00:12:41.620
Hold on.
My minute isn't up yet!

00:12:46.897 --> 00:12:48.262
Harry!

00:12:48.299 --> 00:12:51.063
Grab my hand!

00:12:59.243 --> 00:13:00.540
Harry!

00:13:07.451 --> 00:13:09.442
Lieutenant Hogan!

00:13:09.520 --> 00:13:11.283
Kes! Over here!

00:13:22.632 --> 00:13:23.860
Torres to Bridge.

00:13:23.900 --> 00:13:25.697
Ensign Kim is dead.

00:13:25.735 --> 00:13:27.828
Kes just disappeared.

00:13:27.871 --> 00:13:29.031
Disappeared?!

00:13:29.072 --> 00:13:30.198
I can't explain it.

00:13:30.240 --> 00:13:33.732
She just vanished.

00:13:33.776 --> 00:13:36.244
There seems to be
some kind of spatial rift

00:13:36.279 --> 00:13:38.076
right where she disappeared.

00:13:38.114 --> 00:13:40.241
Can you determine
where it leads?

00:13:40.283 --> 00:13:41.841
Stand by, Bridge.

00:13:46.656 --> 00:13:49.181
I just threw a piece of conduit
into the rift.

00:13:49.225 --> 00:13:51.455
Just as it vanished,
I detected another

00:13:51.494 --> 00:13:53.257
oxygen/nitrogen atmosphere.

00:13:53.296 --> 00:13:54.490
Another atmosphere?

00:13:54.564 --> 00:13:56.964
Whatever's on
the other side of that rift

00:13:57.000 --> 00:13:59.127
there's air...
maybe Kes is still alive.

00:14:02.639 --> 00:14:03.606
Get out of there, Torres.

00:14:03.640 --> 00:14:04.607
The hull breach is widening.

00:14:04.641 --> 00:14:05.733
I'm going to evacuate
the entire deck.

00:14:06.943 --> 00:14:09.036
You don't have to tell me twice.

00:14:09.078 --> 00:14:11.046
The main computer core
is failing.

00:14:11.080 --> 00:14:12.877
Switching to backup processors.

00:14:13.883 --> 00:14:16.113
Chakotay, are you ready
to magnetize the hull?

00:14:16.152 --> 00:14:17.141
Stand by.

00:14:17.186 --> 00:14:18.949
I'm having trouble with
the alignment module.

00:14:18.988 --> 00:14:20.512
Try remodulating
the field emitter.

00:14:22.825 --> 00:14:24.190
Chakotay.

00:14:25.194 --> 00:14:27.162
I've got alignment.

00:14:27.196 --> 00:14:29.426
Magnetizing the hull.

00:14:38.908 --> 00:14:39.966
I think it worked.

00:14:40.009 --> 00:14:41.203
Let's hope so.

00:14:41.244 --> 00:14:43.576
I want a full damage report
from all decks.

00:14:43.613 --> 00:14:45.171
Are you all right, Captain?

00:14:45.214 --> 00:14:46.806
It's just a scratch.

00:14:46.849 --> 00:14:47.907
It's more than a scratch.
Maybe you should go...

00:14:47.951 --> 00:14:49.077
I'm fine, Lieutenant.

00:14:49.118 --> 00:14:51.052
Damage reports are coming in.

00:14:51.087 --> 00:14:53.954
The hull breach
on Deck 15 has widened

00:14:53.990 --> 00:14:56.117
to include Deck 14, Section 12.

00:14:56.159 --> 00:14:58.593
And there are
632 micro-fractures

00:14:58.628 --> 00:15:00.596
along the hull's infrastructure.

00:15:00.630 --> 00:15:02.530
All primary systems
are off-line.

00:15:02.565 --> 00:15:04.829
We are running
on emergency power only.

00:15:04.867 --> 00:15:07.358
The antimatter supply
has dropped to 18 percent

00:15:07.403 --> 00:15:09.064
and is continuing to fall.

00:15:09.105 --> 00:15:11.573
Warp coils in both
nacelles have fused

00:15:11.607 --> 00:15:12.938
and are inoperative.

00:15:12.976 --> 00:15:15.945
The environmental control
systems are failing.

00:15:15.979 --> 00:15:18.777
15 crew members have
been seriously wounded

00:15:18.815 --> 00:15:19.907
with plasma burns.

00:15:19.949 --> 00:15:21.849
27 experienced other injuries.

00:15:21.884 --> 00:15:24.648
The Doctor is setting up
triage facilities

00:15:24.687 --> 00:15:26.552
in Sick Bay and Holodeck 2.

00:15:26.589 --> 00:15:28.614
I must also regretfully report

00:15:28.658 --> 00:15:31.525
that Ensign Wildman's baby
did not survive.

00:15:35.665 --> 00:15:38.065
I want an Engineering team
to seal those micro-fractures

00:15:38.101 --> 00:15:39.090
before they become breaches.

00:15:39.135 --> 00:15:40.102
Aye, Captain.

00:15:40.136 --> 00:15:41.125
Mr. Paris, grab

00:15:41.170 --> 00:15:42.694
a medical tricorder
and go assist the Doctor.

00:15:42.739 --> 00:15:43.899
Right.

00:15:43.940 --> 00:15:45.430
Commander, you have the Bridge.
I'm going

00:15:45.475 --> 00:15:46.442
to go talk to Ensign Wildman.

00:15:46.476 --> 00:15:47.465
Maybe I can help...

00:15:55.852 --> 00:15:58.343
The magnetic field
is collapsing!

00:15:58.388 --> 00:16:00.356
The hull is depolarizing!

00:16:05.428 --> 00:16:07.623
The fire suppression
system is out.

00:16:07.663 --> 00:16:10.359
Warning. Hull breach on Deck 1.

00:16:10.400 --> 00:16:12.300
Emergency force fields
inoperative.

00:16:12.335 --> 00:16:14.326
Everybody out!
Go! Go! Go!

00:16:17.473 --> 00:16:19.236
Hurry, Captain!

00:16:19.275 --> 00:16:21.004
I'm trying
to reroute emergency power

00:16:21.044 --> 00:16:23.137
to the field emitters!

00:16:25.448 --> 00:16:26.881
Captain!

00:16:26.916 --> 00:16:29.009
I can seal this breach!

00:16:38.161 --> 00:16:40.595
Captain, let's go!

00:16:49.439 --> 00:16:51.566
Captain?

00:16:51.607 --> 00:16:53.939
Ensign Kim, scan the Bridge.

00:16:55.611 --> 00:16:57.772
I just saw myself
cross the Bridge

00:16:57.814 --> 00:17:00.044
and enter that turbolift.

00:17:00.083 --> 00:17:04.315
It was very faint...
almost like a ghost image...

00:17:04.353 --> 00:17:05.980
and I looked like hell.

00:17:07.256 --> 00:17:08.814
Captain,

00:17:08.858 --> 00:17:11.053
there was a minor spatial
fluctuation on the Bridge,

00:17:11.094 --> 00:17:13.289
but it was only there
for a millisecond.

00:17:13.329 --> 00:17:15.160
Bridge to Engineering.

00:17:15.198 --> 00:17:16.426
B'Elanna, how long
until we can use

00:17:16.532 --> 00:17:17.965
the main sensor array?

00:17:18.000 --> 00:17:19.160
Another three hours.

00:17:19.202 --> 00:17:21.568
We're only about halfway through
the proton burst procedure.

00:17:21.604 --> 00:17:23.037
See if you can speed up
the process.

00:17:23.072 --> 00:17:25.836
We need the sensors as soon
as possible.

00:17:25.875 --> 00:17:26.864
Understood.

00:17:26.909 --> 00:17:28.774
Mr. Kim, modify a tricorder

00:17:28.811 --> 00:17:30.904
to scan for spatial anomalies.

00:17:30.947 --> 00:17:33.745
Go over every centimeter
of this Bridge.

00:17:33.783 --> 00:17:35.444
Examine the sensor logs

00:17:35.485 --> 00:17:38.215
from our trip through
the plasma drift.

00:17:38.254 --> 00:17:40.051
Look for anything unusual.

00:17:40.089 --> 00:17:41.454
I'll be in Sick Bay.

00:17:41.524 --> 00:17:43.151
Aye, Captain.

00:17:47.964 --> 00:17:49.226
Good news, Ensign.

00:17:49.265 --> 00:17:51.460
Our baby is perfectly healthy.

00:17:51.534 --> 00:17:55.231
There's no sign of
any inter-species abnormalities.

00:17:55.271 --> 00:17:56.670
"Our" baby.

00:17:56.706 --> 00:17:58.173
A figure of speech.

00:17:58.207 --> 00:18:00.937
I am, in part, responsible
for bringing her into the world.

00:18:02.879 --> 00:18:05.973
You may hold her now.

00:18:06.015 --> 00:18:07.482
Hello, there.

00:18:11.521 --> 00:18:14.012
Congratulations, Samantha.

00:18:15.825 --> 00:18:17.986
She's adorable.

00:18:18.027 --> 00:18:19.255
Have you thought of a name?

00:18:19.295 --> 00:18:20.319
Not yet.

00:18:20.363 --> 00:18:22.923
I really thought
it would be a boy.

00:18:22.965 --> 00:18:25.092
Let me know
as soon as you decide.

00:18:25.134 --> 00:18:27.602
I've been making
a blanket for her.

00:18:27.637 --> 00:18:29.901
All that's missing
is an initial.

00:18:33.643 --> 00:18:35.474
Get some rest.

00:18:36.913 --> 00:18:38.938
How's our other patient doing?

00:18:38.981 --> 00:18:40.573
She's still unconscious.

00:18:40.616 --> 00:18:42.447
I ran a microcellular scan.

00:18:42.485 --> 00:18:44.976
We're almost identical
in every way.

00:18:45.021 --> 00:18:46.386
Almost?

00:18:46.422 --> 00:18:49.255
There's a slight phase shift
in their DNA.

00:18:49.292 --> 00:18:52.784
Do you have any theory
about where she came from?

00:18:52.828 --> 00:18:55.194
Not yet,
but I intend to find out.

00:18:55.231 --> 00:18:56.425
Can you wake her?

00:18:56.465 --> 00:18:57.898
I believe so.

00:18:57.934 --> 00:18:59.458
Good...

00:18:59.569 --> 00:19:01.594
because I think
she's going to have

00:19:01.637 --> 00:19:03.298
an interesting story to tell.

00:19:08.978 --> 00:19:12.414
I was running through the
corridor with my medkit...

00:19:12.515 --> 00:19:16.417
Deck 15...

00:19:16.485 --> 00:19:19.318
and then, suddenly,

00:19:19.355 --> 00:19:21.846
I felt dizzy

00:19:21.891 --> 00:19:23.654
and my vision started to blur.

00:19:26.128 --> 00:19:29.029
After that,
I don't remember anything

00:19:29.065 --> 00:19:31.431
until you woke me up
just now.

00:19:31.500 --> 00:19:33.593
You were found unconscious
down on Deck 15

00:19:33.636 --> 00:19:35.160
holding a medkit.

00:19:35.204 --> 00:19:38.071
We also found this
lying next to you.

00:19:38.107 --> 00:19:40.837
It's a piece of damaged conduit.

00:19:40.876 --> 00:19:45.575
Our analysis shows
it's from Voyager, Deck 15,

00:19:45.614 --> 00:19:48.811
Section 29-Alpha, Bulkhead 052...

00:19:48.851 --> 00:19:51.979
but there's no damage to Deck 15
or anywhere else on this ship.

00:19:52.021 --> 00:19:55.218
There was massive damage
to Deck 15.

00:19:55.257 --> 00:19:57.122
The evidence
would seem to suggest

00:19:57.159 --> 00:19:59.252
that you've come
from a different ship...

00:19:59.295 --> 00:20:01.286
a different Voyager.

00:20:02.665 --> 00:20:05.395
We did find a spatial
rift on Deck 15.

00:20:05.434 --> 00:20:07.698
It's possible that it
somehow connects us

00:20:07.736 --> 00:20:08.930
to this other Voyager.

00:20:08.971 --> 00:20:11.201
If you're right,
where is the other ship?

00:20:11.240 --> 00:20:13.333
A parallel universe?
Another dimension?

00:20:13.375 --> 00:20:14.603
Another point in time?

00:20:14.643 --> 00:20:16.042
I'm not sure.

00:20:16.078 --> 00:20:18.945
Almost everything about
the Voyager Kes described

00:20:18.981 --> 00:20:20.209
is identical to ours.

00:20:20.249 --> 00:20:23.480
We've had similar experiences,
similar personal histories.

00:20:23.586 --> 00:20:27.955
We both entered a plasma cloud
to avoid the Vidiians.

00:20:27.990 --> 00:20:30.686
Both of our engines stalled
as we left the cloud,

00:20:30.726 --> 00:20:33.695
which caused both of our
antimatter supplies to drain

00:20:33.729 --> 00:20:36.061
and then we both decided
to keep our engines running

00:20:36.098 --> 00:20:39.067
by emitting proton bursts...

00:20:39.101 --> 00:20:43.037
but after that,
our experiences diverged.

00:20:44.406 --> 00:20:47.739
We started emitting
the proton bursts.

00:20:47.776 --> 00:20:49.073
They didn't.

00:20:49.111 --> 00:20:51.011
Our ship was being damaged
by proton bursts.

00:20:51.046 --> 00:20:53.776
We couldn't figure out
where they were coming from.

00:20:53.816 --> 00:20:55.477
That's more than a coincidence.

00:20:55.518 --> 00:20:56.849
Janeway to Engineering.

00:20:56.886 --> 00:21:00.083
B'Elanna, I want you to stop
the proton bursts immediately.

00:21:00.122 --> 00:21:01.783
But if we stop now,
the power levels will drop...

00:21:01.824 --> 00:21:03.985
I'll explain later, Lieutenant.

00:21:04.026 --> 00:21:05.721
Understood.

00:21:05.761 --> 00:21:08.423
I don't know how...

00:21:08.464 --> 00:21:11.456
but there's another
Voyager out there

00:21:11.567 --> 00:21:13.228
and I intend to find it.

00:21:18.073 --> 00:21:19.597
We analyzed the sensor logs

00:21:19.642 --> 00:21:21.109
from our trip
through the plasma cloud.

00:21:21.143 --> 00:21:22.735
We couldn't find
anything unusual

00:21:22.778 --> 00:21:25.838
until we ran
a quantum-level analysis.

00:21:25.881 --> 00:21:27.280
Remember that subspace
turbulence we hit

00:21:27.316 --> 00:21:28.340
just before we left the cloud?

00:21:28.384 --> 00:21:29.351
Yes.

00:21:29.385 --> 00:21:31.512
Well, watch what happens.

00:21:33.822 --> 00:21:36.848
At first, we thought it was
a sensor aberration,

00:21:36.892 --> 00:21:39.383
but they were in perfect
calibration at the time.

00:21:39.428 --> 00:21:41.157
So I ran a
multispectral analysis

00:21:41.197 --> 00:21:42.664
on the subspace turbulence.

00:21:42.698 --> 00:21:44.461
It was more
than just turbulence.

00:21:44.500 --> 00:21:46.400
It was some kind
of divergence field.

00:21:46.435 --> 00:21:47.732
And the moment
we passed through it,

00:21:47.770 --> 00:21:49.499
all of our sensor
readings doubled.

00:21:49.605 --> 00:21:52.130
Mass, energy output,
bio-signatures... everything.

00:21:52.174 --> 00:21:54.699
Every particle
of matter on the ship

00:21:54.743 --> 00:21:56.404
seems to have been
duplicated in that instant.

00:21:56.445 --> 00:21:58.879
So where's the other ship?

00:21:58.914 --> 00:22:00.643
As strange as it sounds,
Captain,

00:22:00.683 --> 00:22:02.207
according to these readings,

00:22:02.251 --> 00:22:04.446
another Voyager is
right here, right now,

00:22:04.520 --> 00:22:07.956
occupying the same point
in space-time that we are.

00:22:09.758 --> 00:22:11.783
Quantum theorists
at Kent State University

00:22:11.827 --> 00:22:14.557
ran an experiment in which
a single particle of matter

00:22:14.597 --> 00:22:17.327
was duplicated using the
divergence of subspace fields...

00:22:17.366 --> 00:22:20.164
a spatial scission.

00:22:20.202 --> 00:22:22.602
If the same forces were at work
inside the plasma cloud,

00:22:22.638 --> 00:22:24.606
they may have duplicated
every particle of matter

00:22:24.640 --> 00:22:25.607
on Voyager.

00:22:25.641 --> 00:22:28.474
Matter... but not antimatter.

00:22:28.544 --> 00:22:29.476
Captain?

00:22:29.545 --> 00:22:31.479
In that Kent State experiment,

00:22:31.513 --> 00:22:33.777
they were able
to duplicate normal matter,

00:22:33.816 --> 00:22:35.784
but when they tried to duplicate
antimatter particles,

00:22:35.818 --> 00:22:38.116
the experiment failed.

00:22:38.153 --> 00:22:42.351
So the antimatter on the ships
wasn't duplicated.

00:22:42.391 --> 00:22:45.383
Both engines have been
trying to draw power

00:22:45.427 --> 00:22:47.622
from a single source
of antimatter.

00:22:47.663 --> 00:22:49.790
Like Siamese twins
linked at the chest,

00:22:49.832 --> 00:22:51.663
with only one heart.

00:22:51.700 --> 00:22:53.099
So what do we do?

00:22:53.135 --> 00:22:55.069
I don't know,
but whatever it is,

00:22:55.104 --> 00:22:57.095
we're going to have
to coordinate it

00:22:57.139 --> 00:22:58.265
with the other ship.

00:22:58.307 --> 00:23:00.002
Start working on a way
to communicate with them.

00:23:00.042 --> 00:23:01.009
Right.

00:23:01.043 --> 00:23:03.443
The only link we know of
is on Deck 15...

00:23:03.545 --> 00:23:04.671
the spatial rift.

00:23:04.713 --> 00:23:07.807
We're going to need a way
to send Kes back through safely.

00:23:07.850 --> 00:23:10.444
We could rig a portable
phase discriminator.

00:23:10.519 --> 00:23:12.749
It might protect her
from the spatial transition.

00:23:12.788 --> 00:23:14.449
Get on it.

00:23:16.325 --> 00:23:19.055
When can I start breast feeding?

00:23:19.094 --> 00:23:20.061
Right away.

00:23:20.095 --> 00:23:21.585
However, I should forewarn you

00:23:21.630 --> 00:23:24.793
that her incisors will erupt
within three to four weeks.

00:23:24.833 --> 00:23:28.030
Since your skin lacks
the scales of a Ktarian,

00:23:28.070 --> 00:23:31.062
we'll have
to discuss alternatives.

00:23:31.106 --> 00:23:32.403
When can I take her home?

00:23:32.441 --> 00:23:34.306
In 24 hours.

00:23:34.343 --> 00:23:35.970
I want to observe the infant
to make sure

00:23:36.011 --> 00:23:38.275
there's no more damage
to her cell membranes.

00:23:38.314 --> 00:23:40.748
You're welcome to stay the night
so you may be with her.

00:23:40.783 --> 00:23:41.943
I'd like that.

00:23:42.985 --> 00:23:44.714
Hey... what's the matter?

00:23:52.061 --> 00:23:54.859
Congratulations, Ensign...

00:23:54.897 --> 00:23:56.660
it's a girl.

00:23:56.699 --> 00:23:57.893
I've stabilized
my imaging array,

00:23:57.933 --> 00:23:59.093
but it could go out
at any time.

00:23:59.134 --> 00:24:00.999
Doctor, her cell membranes
are losing cohesion.

00:24:01.036 --> 00:24:02.970
Try remodulating
the osmotic pressure.

00:24:03.005 --> 00:24:03.972
No effect.

00:24:04.006 --> 00:24:04.973
Again.

00:24:05.007 --> 00:24:06.133
Nothing.

00:24:06.175 --> 00:24:07.938
My baby, she's going
to die, isn't she?

00:24:07.976 --> 00:24:09.568
I'm sorry, Ensign.

00:24:09.611 --> 00:24:11.408
She's going to die, isn't she?

00:24:12.881 --> 00:24:15.315
Kes...

00:24:15.351 --> 00:24:17.148
Kes?

00:24:19.121 --> 00:24:20.918
Are you all right?

00:24:20.956 --> 00:24:22.981
Yes.

00:24:23.025 --> 00:24:26.119
It's just...
the baby's crying.

00:24:26.161 --> 00:24:28.459
It was like a bad memory.

00:24:28.497 --> 00:24:30.055
What do you mean?

00:24:30.099 --> 00:24:31.930
On my Voyager,

00:24:31.967 --> 00:24:36.267
during the delivery,
there were complications.

00:24:36.305 --> 00:24:38.637
We performed a fetal transport.

00:24:38.674 --> 00:24:40.141
The same thing happened here.

00:24:40.175 --> 00:24:41.665
The transport was successful.

00:24:41.710 --> 00:24:46.443
On my ship, the medical systems
were heavily damaged.

00:24:46.482 --> 00:24:48.677
The osmotic pressure therapy
didn't work.

00:24:48.717 --> 00:24:50.241
The baby died.

00:24:50.285 --> 00:24:53.015
I'm sorry to hear that.

00:24:53.055 --> 00:24:54.716
But try to understand,
it wasn't your fault.

00:24:54.757 --> 00:24:56.918
The situation was
out of your control.

00:24:58.794 --> 00:25:00.193
Doctor, I've got
to get back to my ship.

00:25:00.229 --> 00:25:01.196
They need my help.

00:25:01.230 --> 00:25:03.721
The Captain's working on it,
Kes.

00:25:03.766 --> 00:25:08.100
In the meantime,
try to get some rest.

00:25:09.772 --> 00:25:13.606
Besides, I'm sure your Voyager
is also equipped

00:25:13.642 --> 00:25:17.772
with a proficient
Emergency Medical Hologram.

00:25:22.917 --> 00:25:23.849
It's a little harder

00:25:23.885 --> 00:25:26.410
to establish a com link
than I thought, Captain.

00:25:26.454 --> 00:25:28.183
The molecular signature
of the second Voyager

00:25:28.222 --> 00:25:30.281
is slightly out of phase
with our own.

00:25:30.324 --> 00:25:32.918
I can't get visual, audio...
nothing.

00:25:32.960 --> 00:25:35.394
Have you tried remodulating
the com-frequency carrier?

00:25:35.429 --> 00:25:37.727
Five times on 47
different frequencies.

00:25:37.765 --> 00:25:39.096
There has to be a way.

00:25:39.133 --> 00:25:42.193
If they were recalibrating their
carrier wave at the same time...

00:25:42.236 --> 00:25:44.136
so we could match
phase variants...

00:25:44.172 --> 00:25:45.605
would that allow us to connect?

00:25:45.640 --> 00:25:48.268
I think so, but, in order
to get them to do that,

00:25:48.309 --> 00:25:50.470
we'd have to communicate
with them first.

00:25:50.545 --> 00:25:52.137
It's the chicken and the egg.

00:25:52.180 --> 00:25:55.638
Maybe we need something
a little more primitive.

00:25:55.683 --> 00:25:58.777
Is there a signal we could
emit on all subspace bands

00:25:58.820 --> 00:26:00.583
just to get their attention?

00:26:00.621 --> 00:26:04.079
A rotating band pulse
might do it,

00:26:04.125 --> 00:26:05.888
but it wouldn't be much
more than a shrill whistle.

00:26:05.927 --> 00:26:08.395
That might be enough.
Give it a try.

00:26:08.429 --> 00:26:09.418
All right, Captain.

00:26:09.497 --> 00:26:11.397
All of the ship's
command functions

00:26:11.432 --> 00:26:13.798
have been rerouted
to Main Engineering.

00:26:13.835 --> 00:26:15.200
Welcome to the new Bridge.

00:26:15.236 --> 00:26:16.464
Now, let's see about...

00:26:17.505 --> 00:26:18.733
What's that?

00:26:18.773 --> 00:26:19.740
I don't know.

00:26:19.774 --> 00:26:21.298
It's some kind of com emissions

00:26:21.342 --> 00:26:23.003
coming through
all subspace bands.

00:26:23.044 --> 00:26:24.011
Coming from where?

00:26:24.045 --> 00:26:26.070
Good question.
I can't tell.

00:26:26.113 --> 00:26:27.978
But it's got
a Federation signature.

00:26:28.015 --> 00:26:30.176
Try recalibrating
our frequency carrier

00:26:30.218 --> 00:26:31.207
to match it.

00:26:35.122 --> 00:26:36.282
That's it.

00:26:36.324 --> 00:26:37.348
They recalibrated

00:26:37.391 --> 00:26:39.256
and locked onto
our phase variant.

00:26:39.293 --> 00:26:40.760
What kind of communication
can we establish?

00:26:40.795 --> 00:26:42.456
Not much, at this point.

00:26:42.496 --> 00:26:43.929
We can use the emergency
encryption code

00:26:43.965 --> 00:26:44.932
for a short message.

00:26:44.966 --> 00:26:46.160
Not more than five seconds.

00:26:46.200 --> 00:26:47.531
That should be enough.

00:26:50.137 --> 00:26:52.332
That's the emergency code.

00:26:52.373 --> 00:26:55.069
Run it through
an alpha-numeric sequencer.

00:26:58.412 --> 00:27:00.573
I think someone's telling us

00:27:00.615 --> 00:27:05.382
to lock onto a frequency
of 12 gigahertz.

00:27:05.419 --> 00:27:07.410
Do it.

00:27:11.425 --> 00:27:13.416
I'll try to clear it up.

00:27:19.600 --> 00:27:21.158
Captain...

00:27:21.202 --> 00:27:22.829
this isn't an illusion.

00:27:22.870 --> 00:27:24.599
What you're seeing is real,

00:27:24.639 --> 00:27:28.166
but it's going to take
some explaining.

00:27:28.209 --> 00:27:30.404
There are two Voyagers
and two crews?

00:27:30.444 --> 00:27:32.071
That's what I was told.

00:27:32.113 --> 00:27:33.307
Could this possibly be

00:27:33.347 --> 00:27:35.110
some kind of subterfuge,
Captain?

00:27:35.149 --> 00:27:36.207
An alien deception?

00:27:36.250 --> 00:27:37.615
That woman, whoever she is,

00:27:37.652 --> 00:27:40.416
had very specific knowledge
of what happened here...

00:27:40.454 --> 00:27:42.217
the damage
from the proton bursts,

00:27:42.256 --> 00:27:44.121
Wildman's baby,
Kes disappearing.

00:27:44.158 --> 00:27:46.456
She even knew that when
I was 12 years old,

00:27:46.560 --> 00:27:48.824
I walked home in a thunderstorm
over seven kilometers

00:27:48.863 --> 00:27:50.057
because I lost a tennis match.

00:27:50.097 --> 00:27:51.792
And her explanation
of how the ships

00:27:51.832 --> 00:27:55.393
were duplicated was
certainly plausible.

00:27:55.436 --> 00:27:57.063
If it is true,
what do we do about it?

00:27:57.104 --> 00:28:01.438
My... counterpart
has suggested we try

00:28:01.475 --> 00:28:02.601
to merge the two ships...

00:28:02.643 --> 00:28:04.338
recreate the subspace
divergence field

00:28:04.378 --> 00:28:06.278
we passed through
and then depolarize it.

00:28:06.314 --> 00:28:07.906
Both ships would have
to send out

00:28:07.949 --> 00:28:09.917
a massive resonance pulse
from their deflector dishes

00:28:09.951 --> 00:28:11.885
at exactly the same time.

00:28:11.919 --> 00:28:13.216
They may be able to do that,

00:28:13.254 --> 00:28:16.087
but we barely have enough
power for life support.

00:28:16.123 --> 00:28:17.283
How can we get enough

00:28:17.325 --> 00:28:19.384
to send an energy pulse
of that size?

00:28:19.427 --> 00:28:21.793
We could evacuate
all the crew to this deck

00:28:21.829 --> 00:28:23.558
and cut off life support
everywhere else.

00:28:23.597 --> 00:28:26.293
Then we could divert all power
to the deflector dish.

00:28:26.334 --> 00:28:27.699
B'Elanna, reestablish
the com-link

00:28:27.735 --> 00:28:29.032
with the other ship.

00:28:32.173 --> 00:28:34.300
This is Janeway.
What have you decided?

00:28:35.343 --> 00:28:39.074
Captain, we think we can
channel enough energy

00:28:39.113 --> 00:28:40.944
to our deflector dish
to try the merging process.

00:28:40.982 --> 00:28:42.973
Good. When can we start?

00:28:43.017 --> 00:28:44.780
We'll need
at least 15 minutes

00:28:44.819 --> 00:28:46.252
to make our preparations.

00:28:46.287 --> 00:28:47.447
We'll be ready.

00:28:47.555 --> 00:28:50.251
And, Captain...

00:28:50.291 --> 00:28:52.851
we'll only have enough
power to try this once.

00:28:52.893 --> 00:28:54.383
I understand.

00:28:56.964 --> 00:28:59.364
Chakotay, Tuvok, begin
the evacuation process.

00:28:59.400 --> 00:29:00.367
Aye, Captain.

00:29:00.401 --> 00:29:01.663
I'll let the Doctor know

00:29:01.702 --> 00:29:04.398
he'll have to rely
on his backup power supply.

00:29:16.584 --> 00:29:18.415
We're ready, Captain.

00:29:20.654 --> 00:29:21.951
We're standing by, Captain.

00:29:21.989 --> 00:29:24.048
I think you should take the lead
in this operation,

00:29:24.091 --> 00:29:26.116
since you may have
to make allowances

00:29:26.160 --> 00:29:27.889
for your ship's
weakened power systems.

00:29:27.928 --> 00:29:28.895
Acknowledged.

00:29:28.929 --> 00:29:30.055
Lieutenant Torres...

00:29:30.097 --> 00:29:31.291
and Lieutenant Torres...

00:29:31.332 --> 00:29:33.425
charge the deflector dishes.

00:29:35.102 --> 00:29:37.434
Deflector dish charging.

00:29:37.471 --> 00:29:39.439
Capacitance levels
are rising.

00:29:39.540 --> 00:29:40.438
60 percent...

00:29:40.541 --> 00:29:42.566
85 percent...

00:29:42.610 --> 00:29:45.078
98 percent...

00:29:45.112 --> 00:29:47.979
We're ready to create
the subspace divergence field.

00:29:48.015 --> 00:29:50.575
Initiating.

00:29:50.618 --> 00:29:52.677
Power flow nominal, Captain.

00:29:52.720 --> 00:29:56.087
Synchronize computer
event timing.

00:29:56.123 --> 00:29:58.751
Ready to release
depolarization pulse

00:29:58.793 --> 00:30:01.091
on my mark.

00:30:01.128 --> 00:30:03.460
Now.

00:30:11.505 --> 00:30:13.473
The pulses have been
emitted, Captain.

00:30:13.541 --> 00:30:15.372
The fields are starting
to depolarize!

00:30:15.409 --> 00:30:17.377
But we aren't merging.

00:30:17.411 --> 00:30:19.811
In fact, we're going
further out of phase!

00:30:19.847 --> 00:30:21.940
Increase power
to the deflector dish.

00:30:23.284 --> 00:30:25.718
I can't!
Too much plasma backflow.

00:30:25.753 --> 00:30:27.220
If we keep this up,
we're going to lose

00:30:27.254 --> 00:30:29.279
our antimatter connection...
we'll both be destroyed!

00:30:29.323 --> 00:30:30.290
Abort!

00:30:30.324 --> 00:30:31.791
Aborting resonance pulse.

00:30:31.826 --> 00:30:32.793
What went wrong?

00:30:32.827 --> 00:30:34.021
I'm not sure.

00:30:34.061 --> 00:30:35.995
I think the plasma flow
became too turbulent.

00:30:36.030 --> 00:30:37.463
The divergence fields
were so chaotic,

00:30:37.498 --> 00:30:38.760
we couldn't complete
the merging.

00:30:40.167 --> 00:30:41.498
We've lost the com-link,
as well.

00:30:43.471 --> 00:30:48.431
Captain... the antimatter leak,
it's becoming a hemorrhage.

00:30:48.476 --> 00:30:49.966
If we don't start
the proton bursts,

00:30:50.010 --> 00:30:52.376
we'll be completely
drained in 30 minutes.

00:30:52.413 --> 00:30:54.244
The lives of both crews
are at stake here.

00:30:54.281 --> 00:30:55.771
I can't make
unilateral decisions

00:30:55.816 --> 00:30:57.374
that might affect
that other ship.

00:30:57.418 --> 00:30:59.045
Janeway to Kim.

00:30:59.086 --> 00:31:01.054
Is the spatial rift
still stable?

00:31:01.088 --> 00:31:02.055
I think so, Captain.

00:31:02.089 --> 00:31:03.681
And I've rigged
a phase discriminator.

00:31:03.724 --> 00:31:05.453
Kes should be able
to go back safely.

00:31:05.559 --> 00:31:07.151
Rig another one, Ensign.

00:31:07.194 --> 00:31:08.752
I'm going with her.

00:31:14.334 --> 00:31:16.996
This should protect you
from the spatial transition.

00:31:17.036 --> 00:31:19.163
Keep trying to reestablish
a com-link between the ships.

00:31:19.205 --> 00:31:20.297
I will, but remember

00:31:20.340 --> 00:31:22.331
we have fewer than 30 minutes
of antimatter left.

00:31:22.375 --> 00:31:24.468
Whatever you do over
there, do it fast.

00:31:24.510 --> 00:31:26.068
Understood.
Are you ready?

00:31:26.112 --> 00:31:27.101
Yes.

00:31:34.687 --> 00:31:36.018
It's gotten worse here.

00:31:36.055 --> 00:31:37.852
Command control is
in Main Engineering.

00:31:37.890 --> 00:31:38.914
Let's go.

00:31:41.361 --> 00:31:44.057
I don't know how else to stop
the antimatter drain

00:31:44.097 --> 00:31:45.496
except with proton bursts.

00:31:45.565 --> 00:31:46.930
We can't do that.

00:31:46.966 --> 00:31:49.958
We'd damage the other ship
just like this one.

00:31:50.003 --> 00:31:51.095
Think, people.

00:31:51.137 --> 00:31:52.468
We need options.

00:31:52.505 --> 00:31:54.439
I agree, Captain.

00:31:56.275 --> 00:31:58.436
And I think we need to talk.

00:32:05.652 --> 00:32:08.120
By my estimates,
our antimatter supply

00:32:08.154 --> 00:32:09.917
will run out in less
than half an hour.

00:32:11.391 --> 00:32:12.551
The attempt to merge our ships

00:32:12.592 --> 00:32:14.287
is throwing us
further out of phase.

00:32:14.327 --> 00:32:15.419
The quantum cohesion

00:32:15.461 --> 00:32:17.554
on both Voyagers
is breaking down.

00:32:18.564 --> 00:32:21.328
Just like the original
Kent State experiment.

00:32:21.367 --> 00:32:23.733
The duplicate atoms couldn't
occupy the same point

00:32:23.770 --> 00:32:25.795
in space-time
for very long before...

00:32:25.838 --> 00:32:28.602
Mutual annihilation.

00:32:28.641 --> 00:32:29.972
What are our options?

00:32:30.009 --> 00:32:31.772
Let's try a different tack.

00:32:31.811 --> 00:32:34.405
Instead of trying to merge
the two ships,

00:32:34.447 --> 00:32:36.574
let's try to separate them.

00:32:36.616 --> 00:32:39.949
Maybe we could divide
the antimatter between us.

00:32:39.986 --> 00:32:41.180
I'm afraid not.

00:32:41.220 --> 00:32:43.017
We've been studying
that theory.

00:32:43.056 --> 00:32:44.956
B'Elanna tells me
that any attempt to disrupt

00:32:44.991 --> 00:32:48.085
the antimatter supply
would destroy us all.

00:32:48.127 --> 00:32:50.220
What about evacuating
your crew to my ship?

00:32:50.263 --> 00:32:52.493
It might get a little crowded,
but we could manage.

00:32:52.598 --> 00:32:54.463
We've been studying that theory,

00:32:54.500 --> 00:32:57.094
and my B'Elanna tells me
that sending any more

00:32:57.136 --> 00:32:59.400
than five to ten people
through the rift

00:32:59.439 --> 00:33:00.963
would radically alter
the atomic balance

00:33:01.007 --> 00:33:02.031
of the two Voyagers.

00:33:02.075 --> 00:33:04.066
We'd both be destroyed.

00:33:07.947 --> 00:33:10.575
Captain, I think you should
return to your ship

00:33:10.616 --> 00:33:13.449
and run a metallurgical
analysis.

00:33:13.553 --> 00:33:16.886
Find out the precise phase
modulation of your hull.

00:33:16.923 --> 00:33:18.584
I'll do the same here.

00:33:18.624 --> 00:33:19.682
Maybe we can find a way

00:33:19.726 --> 00:33:22.251
to realign
the phase displacement.

00:33:22.295 --> 00:33:24.627
You're going
to self-destruct your ship.

00:33:24.664 --> 00:33:26.928
What makes you say that?

00:33:26.966 --> 00:33:30.299
Because that's what I would do
if your Voyager were intact

00:33:30.336 --> 00:33:33.863
and my Voyager were crippled,
my crew wounded or dead.

00:33:33.906 --> 00:33:37.273
I'd sacrifice my ship
so that yours could survive.

00:33:37.310 --> 00:33:39.938
Then I'm glad we agree.

00:33:39.979 --> 00:33:41.469
Go back to your ship.

00:33:41.581 --> 00:33:42.741
I didn't say I agree.

00:33:42.782 --> 00:33:44.044
I said I understand.

00:33:44.083 --> 00:33:46.745
I'm not willing to let you
make that sacrifice yet.

00:33:46.786 --> 00:33:48.777
We haven't explored
all the options.

00:33:48.821 --> 00:33:50.948
Yes, we have,
and we both know it.

00:33:50.990 --> 00:33:52.981
This is my ship and my decision.

00:33:53.025 --> 00:33:53.992
Captain, I'm not
going to let you...

00:33:54.026 --> 00:33:55.050
I've made my decision.

00:33:55.094 --> 00:33:56.584
Please don't make me
call Security

00:33:56.629 --> 00:33:59.621
and have you escorted
off my ship because...

00:33:59.665 --> 00:34:02.930
you know I'll do it.

00:34:04.103 --> 00:34:05.434
All right, I'll go back.

00:34:05.471 --> 00:34:06.733
But give me 15 minutes

00:34:06.773 --> 00:34:08.570
to come up
with another solution.

00:34:08.608 --> 00:34:10.872
After that, it's your decision.

00:34:13.146 --> 00:34:15.614
15 minutes.

00:34:15.648 --> 00:34:18.242
Good luck.

00:34:18.284 --> 00:34:19.683
To both of us.

00:34:26.659 --> 00:34:28.456
Okay, I've managed to
reestablish a com-link

00:34:28.528 --> 00:34:29.460
with the other Voyager.

00:34:29.562 --> 00:34:30.529
Hail them.

00:34:32.431 --> 00:34:34.262
Captain, I've got an idea.

00:34:34.300 --> 00:34:36.097
Actually, it was yours.

00:34:36.135 --> 00:34:37.261
It might be possible

00:34:37.303 --> 00:34:39.168
to realign the phase
displacement between us.

00:34:39.205 --> 00:34:40.194
We don't have time to try it.

00:34:40.239 --> 00:34:41.968
My plan is the only one
that's going to work.

00:34:42.008 --> 00:34:43.532
It's time
that we both accept that.

00:34:44.644 --> 00:34:45.804
We've got a perimeter alert.

00:34:45.845 --> 00:34:49.838
A vessel is approaching,
bearing 005 mark 318.

00:34:49.882 --> 00:34:51.577
They've just dropped out
of warp.

00:34:51.617 --> 00:34:53.107
Can you identify them?

00:34:53.152 --> 00:34:54.380
They're Vidiian, sir.

00:34:56.255 --> 00:34:57.688
Red Alert.

00:34:57.723 --> 00:34:58.587
Shields.

00:34:58.624 --> 00:34:59.591
Still off-line.

00:34:59.625 --> 00:35:01.422
Captain, we're picking up
a Vidiian ship

00:35:01.460 --> 00:35:02.427
heading this way.

00:35:02.495 --> 00:35:03.689
Can you see them, too?

00:35:03.729 --> 00:35:04.696
Yes.

00:35:04.730 --> 00:35:05.992
Do you have any weapons?

00:35:06.032 --> 00:35:07.522
Stand by. Tuvok?

00:35:07.567 --> 00:35:08.534
Negative, Captain.

00:35:08.568 --> 00:35:09.626
We had to reroute power

00:35:09.669 --> 00:35:11.330
to compensate
for the antimatter loss.

00:35:11.370 --> 00:35:14.032
It would take several hours
to bring weapons back on line.

00:35:18.845 --> 00:35:20.278
What is it?

00:35:20.313 --> 00:35:23.908
Their ship seems to be trapped
in some sort of spatial flux.

00:35:23.950 --> 00:35:25.781
- Have they detected us?
- Yes,

00:35:25.818 --> 00:35:27.945
but they can't
raise their shields.

00:35:27.987 --> 00:35:30.012
And it appears that whatever
is happening to them

00:35:30.056 --> 00:35:32.889
has disrupted
their weapon systems.

00:35:32.925 --> 00:35:34.722
Load a hyperthermic charge.

00:35:38.197 --> 00:35:39.323
Fire.

00:35:39.365 --> 00:35:42.266
Captain, they have fired
an energy weapon.

00:35:42.301 --> 00:35:43.825
All hands, brace for impact.

00:35:43.870 --> 00:35:46.805
Damage control teams
stand by.

00:35:51.844 --> 00:35:53.038
What happened?

00:35:53.079 --> 00:35:54.569
They couldn't have missed.

00:35:54.614 --> 00:35:55.672
Maybe they hit
the other Voyager.

00:35:55.715 --> 00:35:56.682
Hail them.

00:35:56.716 --> 00:35:58.377
I've lost the com-link again.

00:35:58.417 --> 00:36:00.783
Try to get it back.

00:36:09.095 --> 00:36:11.757
We have destroyed
their weapons array.

00:36:11.797 --> 00:36:14.527
Maneuver us
to within grappling range.

00:36:22.441 --> 00:36:26.434
They are cutting an access route
through the hull on Deck 5.

00:36:56.507 --> 00:36:57.906
Vulcan, male.

00:36:57.942 --> 00:37:00.103
Phaser blast damaged
the right kidney,

00:37:00.144 --> 00:37:01.304
but the other organs
are healthy.

00:37:01.345 --> 00:37:03.006
Begin with them.

00:37:24.335 --> 00:37:27.099
I've erected an emergency
force field around Sick Bay.

00:37:27.137 --> 00:37:28.570
That should hold them off
for awhile.

00:37:28.606 --> 00:37:29.766
I won't let them take my baby.

00:37:29.807 --> 00:37:31.434
It's going to be all right,
Ensign.

00:37:31.475 --> 00:37:33.875
Give her to me and I'll hide
her inside an access port.

00:37:33.911 --> 00:37:35.105
If they do break in,
it's unlikely

00:37:35.145 --> 00:37:36.407
they'll look for anyone there.

00:37:38.482 --> 00:37:39.449
Trust me, Ensign.

00:37:39.550 --> 00:37:41.575
I won't let anyone
touch our baby.

00:37:41.619 --> 00:37:42.711
Mama will see you soon.

00:37:42.753 --> 00:37:45.153
Lieutenant, give me a hand.

00:37:45.189 --> 00:37:46.156
Move this.

00:37:46.190 --> 00:37:47.418
We're going to have to cut away

00:37:47.458 --> 00:37:49.016
the internal circuitry
to make room...

00:37:50.060 --> 00:37:51.027
Vidiians.

00:37:51.061 --> 00:37:52.255
They're using
some kind of disrupter

00:37:52.296 --> 00:37:53.957
to break down the force field.

00:37:57.134 --> 00:37:58.795
The force field's down.

00:38:02.139 --> 00:38:03.538
Commander.

00:38:03.574 --> 00:38:05.565
They've got everything
below Deck 5

00:38:05.609 --> 00:38:06.769
and I don't know
how much longer

00:38:06.810 --> 00:38:08.209
we can keep them away
from the Bridge.

00:38:08.245 --> 00:38:10.770
Mr. Kim, how many Vidiians
are there on the ship?

00:38:10.814 --> 00:38:13.078
347, and more are boarding.

00:38:13.117 --> 00:38:14.584
We're outnumbered
two to one.

00:38:14.618 --> 00:38:16.643
I've got an incoming
subspace signal.

00:38:16.687 --> 00:38:18.018
It's from the other Voyager.

00:38:18.055 --> 00:38:19.420
They must've reestablished
the com-link.

00:38:19.523 --> 00:38:20.854
On screen.

00:38:22.359 --> 00:38:24.953
Captain, this com-link
might not last much longer.

00:38:24.995 --> 00:38:26.257
What's happening over there?

00:38:26.297 --> 00:38:27.730
We've been boarded.

00:38:27.765 --> 00:38:31.223
The Vidiians are on the verge
of taking over our ship.

00:38:31.268 --> 00:38:32.428
Are they on yours?

00:38:32.469 --> 00:38:35.165
No. We don't think
they can detect our ship.

00:38:35.205 --> 00:38:37.799
Captain, we can have
a security detachment

00:38:37.841 --> 00:38:39.399
cross the spatial rift
and board your ship

00:38:39.443 --> 00:38:42.003
within five minutes.

00:38:42.046 --> 00:38:44.446
No. If we do that,

00:38:44.548 --> 00:38:47.984
the Vidiians might become aware
of your Voyager.

00:38:48.018 --> 00:38:50.452
That would put both ships
at risk.

00:38:50.487 --> 00:38:53.217
We can't just stand by
and let you all be killed.

00:38:53.257 --> 00:38:55.851
I'm not about
to let that happen.

00:38:55.893 --> 00:38:58.760
I'll destroy this ship.

00:38:58.796 --> 00:39:02.323
I don't suppose there's any way
I can change your mind.

00:39:02.366 --> 00:39:04.561
I know how stubborn you can be.

00:39:04.601 --> 00:39:06.296
True.

00:39:06.337 --> 00:39:08.862
But there is something else
I can do for you.

00:39:08.906 --> 00:39:11.397
I'm going to send Harry Kim
through the rift

00:39:11.442 --> 00:39:13.034
with Ensign Wildman's baby.

00:39:13.077 --> 00:39:15.671
Somehow, it seems only fair.

00:39:15.713 --> 00:39:17.874
We'll be waiting for them.

00:39:17.915 --> 00:39:20.281
Just make me a promise,
Kathryn.

00:39:20.317 --> 00:39:22.615
Get your crew home.

00:39:22.653 --> 00:39:27.147
I will.
I will.

00:39:30.561 --> 00:39:32.153
Harry, you've got five minutes.

00:39:32.196 --> 00:39:33.163
Get the baby.

00:39:33.197 --> 00:39:34.289
But, Captain...

00:39:34.331 --> 00:39:35.923
Move it, Ensign!
That's an order!

00:39:41.805 --> 00:39:45.297
Computer, initiate
the self-destruct sequence.

00:39:45.342 --> 00:39:48.641
Authorization:
Janeway-pi-one-one-zero.

00:39:48.679 --> 00:39:52.706
Set at five minutes
and mute voice warnings.

00:39:57.121 --> 00:39:58.611
Enable.

00:39:58.655 --> 00:40:00.452
Warning.

00:40:00.557 --> 00:40:03.355
Self-destruct sequence
has been initiated.

00:40:03.394 --> 00:40:07.330
Warp core overload
in four minutes, 55 seconds.

00:40:07.364 --> 00:40:10.197
There will be
no further audio warnings.

00:40:16.673 --> 00:40:18.231
Ocampa, female.

00:40:18.275 --> 00:40:19.799
The organs are healthy.

00:40:19.843 --> 00:40:22.403
She has an extremely high rate
of tissue regeneration.

00:40:22.446 --> 00:40:23.708
Extract her pelvic ridge.

00:40:23.747 --> 00:40:26.580
We'll analyze the bone marrow
for phage resistance.

00:40:28.452 --> 00:40:30.181
The others are human.

00:40:30.220 --> 00:40:32.620
My scans indicate
their pancreatic tissues

00:40:32.656 --> 00:40:34.783
are well-suited for transplant.

00:40:34.825 --> 00:40:36.019
Begin the extraction procedure.

00:40:36.060 --> 00:40:37.857
Shh.

00:40:40.964 --> 00:40:42.727
This one... a female human.

00:40:42.766 --> 00:40:44.256
She's recently given birth.

00:40:44.301 --> 00:40:45.495
Are you certain?

00:40:45.602 --> 00:40:48.503
Yes. Her hemo-uterine levels
are far above normal.

00:40:48.572 --> 00:40:49.664
Where's the infant?

00:40:49.706 --> 00:40:52.539
Set your bio-probe
to maximum. Find it.

00:40:53.577 --> 00:40:54.669
Shh... shh, shh, shh, shh.

00:41:23.240 --> 00:41:24.639
No!

00:41:24.675 --> 00:41:27.041
Ensign Kim, is that you?

00:41:27.077 --> 00:41:28.374
Doc.

00:41:28.412 --> 00:41:29.743
Am I glad to see you.

00:41:29.780 --> 00:41:31.179
Have we retaken the ship?

00:41:31.215 --> 00:41:34.480
No. Actually, the Captain's put
the ship on self-destruct.

00:41:34.585 --> 00:41:36.917
She ordered me to take the baby
and go to the other Voyager.

00:41:36.954 --> 00:41:39.081
Well, I guess
you'd better hurry then.

00:41:40.524 --> 00:41:41.991
Good-bye, Doc.

00:41:42.025 --> 00:41:44.585
Ensign, tell my counterpart

00:41:44.628 --> 00:41:46.994
that I've corrected all
signs of hemocythemia.

00:41:47.030 --> 00:41:48.019
He'll know what that means.

00:41:48.065 --> 00:41:49.191
Will do.

00:41:56.106 --> 00:41:58.700
Hello.

00:41:58.742 --> 00:42:01.472
I'm Captain Kathryn Janeway.

00:42:01.512 --> 00:42:03.207
Welcome to the Bridge.

00:42:03.247 --> 00:42:04.874
Commander!

00:42:21.031 --> 00:42:22.293
It's about time.

00:42:22.332 --> 00:42:23.458
Tuvok to Janeway.

00:42:23.567 --> 00:42:25.592
Ensign Kim has made it
through the rift.

00:42:25.636 --> 00:42:27.467
With the infant.

00:42:27.504 --> 00:42:29.096
Acknowledged.

00:42:29.139 --> 00:42:32.404
Captain, the Vidiian ship
has been destroyed.

00:42:35.078 --> 00:42:36.340
So has the other Voyager.

00:42:42.419 --> 00:42:46.617
Captain's Log, Stardate 49548.7.

00:42:46.657 --> 00:42:49.785
There are no signs
of any pursuing Vidiian vessels

00:42:49.826 --> 00:42:52.317
and we have resumed
a course toward home.

00:42:54.364 --> 00:42:55.729
Repair efforts are underway.

00:42:55.766 --> 00:42:57.825
Lieutenant Torres estimates
we'll be able

00:42:57.868 --> 00:43:00.029
to return to the Bridge
within three days.

00:43:00.070 --> 00:43:02.903
Good. I'm not sure how much
longer B'Elanna can tolerate

00:43:02.940 --> 00:43:05.204
my standing over her shoulder
in Engineering.

00:43:05.242 --> 00:43:07.267
Hmm.

00:43:07.311 --> 00:43:10.280
Tuvok, is there something
on your mind?

00:43:10.314 --> 00:43:12.748
I am curious, Captain.

00:43:12.783 --> 00:43:14.375
Before the Vidiians attacked,

00:43:14.418 --> 00:43:16.443
when you were in disagreement
with the other Captain about...

00:43:16.486 --> 00:43:20.286
Would I have given the order
to self-destruct our ship?

00:43:20.324 --> 00:43:23.851
I've gone over that moment
a thousand times in my mind.

00:43:23.894 --> 00:43:27.421
The truth is, yes,
I would've given the order.

00:43:27.464 --> 00:43:31.059
But I will admit,
there was a part of me

00:43:31.101 --> 00:43:33.569
that could see
her point of view.

00:43:33.604 --> 00:43:36.732
One could say that you
were both the doubter

00:43:36.773 --> 00:43:38.468
and the doubted.

00:43:38.542 --> 00:43:40.772
I do not envy
the paradox of logic

00:43:40.811 --> 00:43:43.302
you were faced with
in that situation.

00:43:43.347 --> 00:43:45.440
Neither did I.

00:43:45.482 --> 00:43:47.609
And neither did she.

00:44:00.564 --> 00:44:02.293
Thank you.

00:44:02.332 --> 00:44:04.197
Thank you so much.

00:44:04.234 --> 00:44:05.633
You're welcome.

00:44:05.669 --> 00:44:07.796
But you should also
thank the Doctor.

00:44:07.838 --> 00:44:10.966
It was his counterpart
who saved her from the Vidiians.

00:44:11.008 --> 00:44:12.532
I'm not surprised.

00:44:12.576 --> 00:44:15.841
I am programmed to be heroic
when the need arises.

00:44:15.879 --> 00:44:18.814
By the way, Ensign,
this other Doctor...

00:44:18.849 --> 00:44:20.441
did he have a name?

00:44:20.484 --> 00:44:22.679
I really didn't
have time to ask.

00:44:22.719 --> 00:44:25.187
Am I allowed to go back to my
temporary Bridge now, Doctor?

00:44:25.222 --> 00:44:26.587
By all means.

00:44:35.165 --> 00:44:37.258
It's good to have you back,
Ensign.

00:44:37.301 --> 00:44:38.268
Thank you.

00:44:38.302 --> 00:44:39.394
I think.

00:44:39.436 --> 00:44:40.767
Something wrong?

00:44:40.804 --> 00:44:42.066
I'm not sure.

00:44:42.105 --> 00:44:44.767
I mean, this isn't
really my ship.

00:44:44.808 --> 00:44:47.072
And you're not really
my Captain,

00:44:47.110 --> 00:44:49.601
and yet, you are,
and there's no difference,

00:44:49.646 --> 00:44:51.910
but I know there's a difference.

00:44:51.948 --> 00:44:53.472
Or is there?

00:44:53.550 --> 00:44:55.484
It's all a little weird.

00:44:55.519 --> 00:44:58.454
Mr. Kim,
we're Starfleet officers.

00:44:58.488 --> 00:45:00.479
Weird is part of the job.
